  "body": "Sizes is hard and debugging it is hard.\r\n\r\nBeing able to automate debugging without implementing [a `sizes` parser](https://github.com/ausi/respimagelint/blob/b327fd2297b4459e7171988237e2dd293370f2c8/src/collector/readData.js#L43) would be nice. I'd like to be able to compare `img.clientWidth` with something (`img.currentSizes`?) that gave the current [source size value](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#source-size-value) in `px`. So, when:\r\n\r\n`window.innerWidth = 1000`\r\n\r\nthis `img`\r\n\r\n```\r\n<img sizes=\"(min-width: 600px) 80vw, 100vw\">\r\n```\r\n\r\nwould have an `currentSizes` (or whatever) of `800`.\r\n",
